     1	# gororoba-quantum agent guide
     2	
     3	This file carries the repository's own rules; the user-level agent guide
     4	supplies what it leaves unstated. CLAUDE.md loads it.
     5	
     6	
     7	## Layout and gates
     8	
     9	The modules run as scripts from gororoba_quantum/ and form no installable
    10	package; requirements.txt pins the tested runtime and pyproject.toml carries
    11	lint and type-check configuration only. [docs/PYTHON.md](docs/PYTHON.md) is the
    12	central documentation hub for all Python interpreters, dependency manifests,
    13	multi-environment audit, library roles and the 362-distribution inventory
    14	([docs/state/hypercomplex-libraries/libraries.md](docs/state/hypercomplex-libraries/libraries.md)).
    15	[ci/AGENTS.md](ci/AGENTS.md) holds the gate machinery: runner and shards, the
    16	gate ledger and premerge cache, the Python and Qiskit pins, replay runtimes, the
    17	Rocq replays and gate cost.
    18	
    19	**Flag review.** Every command whose cost or correctness depends on its
    20	options (solvers, simulators, Python pools, compilers, cloud launchers,
    21	resource limiters) runs only after the review in
    22	[docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md](docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md): its memory and
    23	time limits, threads, environment and every flag checked against the tool's
    24	own help, starting from the best measured combination in that runbook's table
    25	and adding or superseding a row after the run.
    26	
    27	**Pull requests and the audit.** The workflow `pr.yml` runs
    28	`sh ci/pr_checks.sh lint|types|tests|gates` on every pull request push: Ruff
    29	and mypy over ci/, tests/, gororoba_quantum/, scripts/ and kaggle_kernel/,
    30	pytest over tests/ with `-m "not audit"`, and the ci/gates.json gates of at
    31	most 15 measured seconds that the diff from main reaches (a record binding an
    32	edited producer's digest fails there). Branch protection on main requires
    33	the four checks `lint`, `types`, `tests` and `gates` green on the head; with the Codex
    34	review loop they admit a merge ([Merging](#reviews-and-merges)), and no local
    35	gate run or premerge replay is required. Locally, `sh ci/pr_checks.sh tests
    36	PATH` runs the touched tests under the hosted environment; pushing needs no
    37	exhaustive run. `ci.yml` is the audit: every gate, the retained-evidence
    38	replays, the Rocq replays and the ledger, nightly on main and on manual
    39	dispatch ([ci/AGENTS.md](ci/AGENTS.md)). A failing scheduled run updates the
    40	issue "Nightly audit failing" with each failing gate and the claims citing it;
    41	it blocks no unrelated pull request.
    42	
    43	**Code style.** Every Python file a change touches passes, before each push,
    44	through `"$PYTHON" ci/pinned_tool.py TOOL ARGS` (the versions of
    45	ci/requirements-ci.txt):
    46	- `ruff format --target-version py313` (120-column lines from pyproject.toml;
    47	  the Python 3.13 target is the Quantum Inspire interpreter's);
    48	- `ruff check` (pycodestyle, pyflakes, import order, bugbear, pyupgrade, S101);
    49	- `mypy` on the touched files, and over gororoba_quantum/, scripts/, ci/,
    50	  tests/ and kaggle_kernel/ (from gororoba_quantum/: `mypy . ../scripts ../ci
    51	  ../tests ../kaggle_kernel`) when a change alters a signature another module
    52	  imports.
    53	
    54	A gate command run outside ci/run_gates.py needs `PYTHON` exported
    55	(`export PYTHON="${PYTHON:-python3}"`); an unexported assignment expands empty
    56	and every gate exits 127 in 0.0 s. A check raises explicitly and never uses
    57	`assert`, which `python -O` strips. Every CPU-bound loop over independent items
    58	runs through parallel.py, an order-preserving spawn pool, and a serial loop
    59	over such items is a defect review rejects; items that share a seeded generator
    60	draw every item's inputs first, in the generator's order, and then map, so
    61	pooled and serial runs write the same bytes. A classical estimator over many
    62	synthetic replicates (a null calibration, a bootstrap) is batched across
    63	replicates with numpy before it is pooled, and a gate proves the batched path
    64	returns the scalar reference's bits: it keeps the scalar arithmetic order,
    65	repeats `sum()`'s Neumaier compensation and sends every replicate-dependent
    66	`exp` and `** 2` through `math.exp` and `math.pow`
    67	([vectorized-fits.md](docs/runbooks/vectorized-fits.md)). Mock outcomes
    68	(`--native-dry-run` timing) never enter scientific analysis or measured
    69	visualizations. Local shells, CI and Kaggle start Python with
    70	`GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.rtld.optional_static_tls=4096`, which the combined Qiskit
    71	Rust and Aer OpenMP extensions require. A change to live_run.py or
    72	experiments.py also gets a dry run, `"$PYTHON" live_run.py --out
    73	../results/live`, whose audit record lands under results/live/. A change to
    74	`proofs/`, a replay bundle or its receipts follows the Rocq replay of
    75	[ci/AGENTS.md](ci/AGENTS.md#layout-and-gates).
    76	
    77	**Seeds.** Every new random seed, on any provider or simulator, comes from a
    78	quantum random number generator: a numpy or `random` generator seed,
    79	`seed_transpiler`, `seed_simulator`, a Perceval `compilation_seed`, a bootstrap
    80	or null-calibration seed. The ANU QRNG serves first (`"$PYTHON"
    81	scripts/anu_qrng.py draw --out docs/evidence/anu_qrng`, keyed then keyless, no
    82	approval needed); [docs/notes/qrng/README.md](docs/notes/qrng/README.md) holds
    83	the fallback order, quotas, key files and approval rule of every source. The
    84	code or case cites the draw file and the index of every value it takes, in
    85	index order, each value used once. A seed that reproduces a retained record,
    86	an approved plan or a known compiled mesh is an identifier and keeps its value,
    87	because the record's replay and the approved-record comparison depend on it.
    88	The seed follows the job's question, not the circuit: a job that reproduces an
    89	earlier result imports the earlier seed constant by name, and a new job on an
    90	earlier circuit that needs its own randomness (an independent replicate, a
    91	fresh layout or twirl, a new mesh) takes new values from a draw.
    92	`ci/seed_provenance.py`, run by the `tests` check, requires every integer seed
    93	literal in the code directories and in every git-tracked Python file under
    94	docs/ to be a row of ci/reproduction_seeds.json, which only shrinks against
    95	main, or an entry of docs/evidence/qrng_seeds/allocations.json naming a
    96	registered source's draw that no case manifest owns and the index holding that
    97	value. A tracked file that takes a draw value the literal scan cannot key (a
    98	helper alias, a mapping) gets a `reserved` row there instead. A seed a CLI takes
    99	at run time goes through `qrng_seeds.add_seed_argument`, which accepts
   100	`qrng:<draw>#<index>`, the flag's default or `repro:<integer>` and refuses any
   101	other integer; the run record's `seed_source` names the spelling, and the
   102	change that retains a qrng-seeded run adds its ledger row with
   103	`"$PYTHON" ci/seed_provenance.py --add-runtime`.
   104	
   105	## Work planning
   106	
   107	[docs/state/plans.md](docs/state/plans.md) is the planning entry point. JSON records own work status;
   108	Markdown views are generated. Capture ideas cheaply, then record scope, owner, next action and checkable
   109	steps before committing work. Update records when scope changes, work pauses or an obligation closes.
   110	Completion requires scope-bound receipts; scientific claims and provider approvals keep their existing
   111	authorities. Reconcile JSON conflicts by hand, regenerate views and run `scripts/plan_tracker.py check`.
   112	The [operator procedure](docs/runbooks/plan-tracker.md) documents commands and shared-checkout locking.
   113	
   114	## Source library and research replay
   115	
   116	`docs/` owns source notes, retained PDFs, retrieval identities and research
   117	replays, and [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) is the map of every document.
   118	`literature -> docs` preserves recorded paths; new Markdown links use `docs/`. Immutable source ledgers retain their recorded bytes. External-only sources (`redistribution: excluded_without_permission`) keep their reading copies and Markdown transcriptions in the owner's private repository
   119	[gororoba-quantum-documents](https://github.com/Oichkatzelesfrettschen/gororoba-quantum-documents), cloned beside this checkout; `"$PYTHON" scripts/fetch_source_cache.py --missing --from-documents DIR` restores the
   120	ignored `docs/local_source_cache/` from it, and the same command without `--from-documents` fetches the registered URLs.
   121	Only that repository receives those files; [docs/sources/reading-copies.md](docs/sources/reading-copies.md), regenerated by `scripts/source_reading_copies.py` after every registry change, links each one beside its public source. The
   122	`sources` suite in ci/gates.json covers the source registry, the evidence
   123	replays and their checksum ledgers.
   124	
   125	
   126	Changes to proof replay inputs also follow the pinned Rocq replay in
   127	`docs/evidence/folding_proofs/README.md`. Imported paper parser diagnostics
   128	remain source limitations in the registry; checksum admission preserves the
   129	original bytes and differs from a fresh mathematical proof check.
   130	
   131	**Computer algebra.** Exact replays compute in global monomial orderings (`dp`,
   132	`lp`). A local invariant at a point p, such as a tangent cone, multiplicity or
   133	singularity type, comes from the deformation to the normal cone: translate p
   134	to 0, substitute t -> h t, take `sat(I, h)` (an ideal in Singular 4.4, not a
   135	list) and set h = 0. The reduced germ at p is the intersection of the
   136	`minAssGTZ` primes through p, with no prior `radical()`. Local orderings (`ds`,
   137	`tangentcone`) on the A_5 strata ran past an hour at tens of GiB on the shared
   138	host, while the global route takes seconds
   139	([a5-strata-regularity](docs/evidence/a5-strata-regularity/README.md)). A
   140	long Singular or msolve run follows the flag review above.
   141	
   142	## Documents
   143	
   144	[docs/README.md](docs/README.md) is the map and decides where a document
   145	lives; read it before writing one.
   146	
   147	- Extend before adding. A fact has one home; a second area that needs it gets
   148	  a link, and a deduplication merges the fact up to the nearest home every
   149	  reader reaches, never into sibling copies.
