     1	# Orbit stratification, singular loci and normal links of the A_5 rank strata
     2	
     3	`result.json` is the output of [`strata_regularity.py`](strata_regularity.py) `--out`. The record settles roadmap item 4
     4	of [the global classification](../../notes/rank_locus_two_dimension_gap.md#route-to-the-global-classification-roadmap-items-3-8)
     5	for the A_5 zero-divisor set: the singular locus of every piece of every rank stratum, a Whitney stratification of
     6	C^15 whose strata refine the nullity strata, the closure incidences between the strata, and the transverse germ of
     7	every piece along every stratum of nullity at least 8, with the normal link wherever the germ type is identified.
     8	The mechanism is a symmetry group: the rank strata are unions of orbits of
     9	H = G_2(C) x SO(2, C) x C^*, the locus of nullity at least 8 is a union of twelve orbits and the origin, and every
    10	local question along an orbit becomes one computation at one point.
    11	
    12	Seven statements are established:
    13	
    14	1. **Symmetry.** H and the reflection mu' -> -mu' carry every rank locus R_k into itself.
    15	2. **Orbits.** R_8 minus 0 is the disjoint union of the twelve H-orbits of the table below.
    16	3. **Incidences.** The closure of each orbit is the closed set of the table, and the closure order is the order of the
    17	   table's last column. In particular W8 n E8-bar = B9 and W8 n V = V n B9.
    18	4. **Singular loci.** The singular locus of every closure, of V(Q) and of V(G) is the union of orbits listed below.
    19	5. **Nullity 4.** V(Q) is smooth off 0, Sing V(G) = W8 u V, and V(Q) n V(G) is an irreducible normal complete
    20	   intersection of dimension 13, smooth off R_8, where V(Q) and V(G) cross transversally.
    21	6. **Stratification.** The twelve orbits, the origin, the three nullity-4 strata and the nullity-0 stratum form a
    22	   Whitney stratification of C^15; each R_k and each nullity stratum S_k is a union of strata.
    23	7. **Germs and links.** The transverse germ of each closure along each orbit has the invariants of the germ table. At
    24	   x0 = e_1 + e_18 the normal link of R_12 = V u B9 is S^1 disjoint union S^3.
    25	
    26	Every decision is an exact computation: python-flint ranks of rational matrices, and Singular 4.4.1 standard bases,
    27	radicals, saturations and minimal associated primes over Q, all in global orderings. No random draw enters; every point
    28	is an explicit integer vector.
    29	
    30	## Conventions
    31	
    32	The coordinates, split coordinates, pieces and the slice families are those of
    33	[the strata record](../a5-zero-divisor-strata/README.md) and [the equations record](../a5-rank-strata-equations/README.md).
    34	A doubly pure y of A_5 is the vector z' = (u', mu', v') in C^15 in split coordinates, with u', v' in the 7-dimensional
    35	module of the split octonions, eta the invariant form diag(-, -, +, -, +, +, -) and x x y the cross product. R_k is the
    36	closed set of nullity at least k and S_k = R_k minus R_(k+4). Write s = u' + v' and d = u' - v'.
    37	
    38	**Real and complex.** The map y -> z' is an R-linear isomorphism of the doubly pure subspace R^30 onto C^15, and
    39	D_(5,k) is the unit section of the cone S_k. Every statement below is about the complex cones read as real sets:
    40	complex smoothness is real smoothness, a complex orbit of dimension n has real dimension 2n, and the link of a complex
    41	germ of dimension n is a real manifold or stratified space of dimension 2n - 1. All strata are cones under the real
