     1	# Consultation brief: four failed A_5 fiber-cone / Rees computations
     2	
     3	Act as an independent computer-algebra consultant. Read only; write nothing except your final answer.
     4	A Claude analysis agent is writing `first-principles-plan.md` in this directory in parallel; give an
     5	independent view, and where that file already exists, critique it.
     6	
     7	## Read first
     8	- `docs/local/a5-failed-runs/` : `inputs/` (the Singular/msolve inputs), `kaggle-pack-a/`, `azure-vm2/` (logs, memory traces), `probes/`.
     9	- `docs/local/a5-iso-np-h3-analysis/algebra-options.md` and `execution-options.md` (a worked analysis of the sister Iso->N+ degree-3 run, including the Nakayama quadric reduction 969 -> 265 cubic generators).
    10	- `AGENTS.md` section "Computer algebra"; `docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md` (measured flag rows, msolve rows 164-168); `docs/evidence/a5-strata-regularity/README.md`.
    11	
    12	## The failures
    13	1. Kaggle pack A, X+ -> N+ fiber: out of memory after the degree-2 count h2 = 51.
    14	2. Kaggle pack A, X- -> N- fiber: hit the time limit.
    15	3. Kaggle pack A, Iso K2: hit the time limit (partial: 69 relations, K2 degree 23).
    16	4. Azure VM2: E8-bar -> N+ msolve variants crash growing hash tables (~2^28 entries); W8 N- fiber Singular "no more memory" near 80 GiB.
    17	
    18	## Resources
    19	- Host: 16 GiB-cgroup-capped Singular runs are routine; RTX 4070 Ti (12 GiB); multi-core CPU; ~64+ GiB RAM shared.
    20	- Kaggle: 4-vCPU CPU (~30 GiB), T4 x2, TPU v5e kernels, 12 h sessions.
    21	- Azure: FX4mds_v2 (4 vCPU, 84 GiB), cap 4 vCPU per region (eastus, westus2); a new VM needs an approved case.
    22	- GitHub Actions runners (4 vCPU, 16 GiB, 6 h).
    23	- Installed: Singular 4.4.1, Macaulay2, msolve 0.11.0, FLINT 3.6 (+ python-flint), Sage 10.10, giac, LinBox, fflas-ffpack, gfan, CuPy, nvmath, magma-cuda, cuQuantum 26.09.
    24	- Buildable via `~/Github/PKGBUILDs` (Arch makepkg tree; each dir is one package; see its README.md) or AUR/paru: Normaliz, 4ti2, CoCoA-5, msolve master, OSCAR.jl, Macaulay2 packages (FastMinors, ReesAlgebra, MultigradedImplicitization), Gfan, M4RI/M4RIE, any GitHub project we can package.
    25	
