  1395	     M:Module
  1396	       or @ofClass Ideal@
  1397	     f:RingElement
  1398	       an optional element, which is a non-zerodivisor such that $M[f^{-1}]$ is a free module when $M$ is a module, an element in $M$ when $M$ is an ideal
  1399	  Outputs
  1400	     :Ring
  1401	  Description
  1402	   Text
  1403	     Let $M$ be an $R = k[x_1,\ldots,x_n]/J$-module (for example an ideal), and
  1404	     let $mm=ideal vars R = (x_1,\ldots,x_n)$, and suppose that $M$ is a
  1405	     homomorphic image of the free module $F$ with $m+1$ generators. Let $T$ be the Rees algebra of
  1406	     $M$. The call specialFiber(M) returns the ideal $J\subset{} k[w_0,\dots,w_m]$
  1407	     such that $k[w_0,\dots,w_m]/J \cong{} T/mm*T$; that is, $specialFiber(M) =
  1408	     reesIdeal(M)+mm*Sym(F)$. This routine differs from @TO specialFiberIdeal@ in that
  1409	     the ambient ring of the output ideal is $k[w_0,\dots,w_m]$ rather than
  1410	     $R[w_0,\dots,w_m]$. 
  1411	     The coefficient ring $k$ used is always the 
  1412	     @TO ultimate@ @TO2 {coefficientRing, "coefficient ring"} @ of $R$.
  1413	     
  1414	     The name derives from the fact that $Proj(T/mm*T)$ is the special fiber of
  1415	     the blowup of $Spec R$ along the subscheme defined by $I$.
