 12901	     The intersection of these ideals has the same zero-set as the
 12902	     input, i.e., the intersection of the radicals of the list entries
 12903	     coincides with the radical of the input ideal.  In many (but not
 12904	     all!)  cases this is already a decomposition of the radical of the
 12905	     ideal.  (Note however that in general, no inclusion between the
 12906	     input and output ideals holds.)
 12907	     The second, optional argument gives a list of polynomials which
 12908	     define non-zero constraints: those ideals which contain one of the
 12909	     constraint polynomials are omitted from the output list.  Thus the
 12910	     zero set of the intersection of the output ideals is contained in
 12911	     the zero set V of the first input ideal and contains the complement
 12912	     in V of the zero set of the second input ideal.
 12913	‘*Note:*’
 12914	     Not implemented for baserings over real ground fields and Galois
 12915	     fields (that is, only implemented for ground fields for which *note
 12916	     factorize:: is implemented).
